    "notes": "Inspected 47 current views during this construction pass. Three mapped battered brick terraces, pale pierced parapets and supported flights lead to a tapered octagonal shaft with real closed round recesses and simplified wheel-like spokes. The observation crown has eight genuinely open mouths, inward-facing reveals, a supported floor and a closed roof with renderable underside. The pole and geometric red flag/yellow star are visible from both sides. The three setbacks, shaft, crown and flag retain the photographed identity. Fine masonry aging and inscriptions are deliberately omitted rather than copied."
